<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d6" for="edge" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d5" for="edge" attr.name="keywords" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d4" for="edge" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d3" for="edge" attr.name="weight" attr.type="double" />
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;RED BRICK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Red Brick is a historic building that was relocated and faced issues of disrepair, eventually being added to the National Register of Historic Places and considered for redevelopment."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NATIONAL REGISTER OF HISTORIC PLACES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The National Register of Historic Places is an organization that recognized Red Brick as historically significant in 1998."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW YORK CITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New York City is the location where Red Brick is situated, adding context to its historical significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONCERNED RESIDENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Concerned Residents are a group of individuals who added Red Brick to the National Register of Historic Places due to its perceived threat of destruction."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2000S&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2000s saw an interest in redeveloping Red Brick, considering various options such as a community center or senior apartments."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ONTARIO HERITAGE TRUST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ontario Heritage Trust is an organization that manages and preserves heritage properties, including Red Brick School."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SKIP TO CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Skip to content is a feature on the Ontario Heritage Trust website, indicating the organization's digital presence."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOUTH MAIN STREET HISTORIC DISTRICT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"South Main Street Historic District is a historic district that is mentioned in relation to Oregon, highlighting its historical significance."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARTLET RUNEY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bartlet Runey is a notable person who settled in Oregon in 1841, marking the beginning of the town's history."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOWN OF OREGON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Town of Oregon is a location where Bartlet Runey settled in 1841, and the town's history is marked by significant events and figures."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHICAGO AND NORTH WESTERN RAILROAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Chicago and North Western Railroad played a role in naming the town of Oregon in 1864."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROME CORNERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rome Corners is a former name for the settlement that later became known as Oregon."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1841&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1841 marks the year when Bartlet Runey settled in Oregon, initiating the town's history."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1843&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1843 marks the year when the first house was constructed in Oregon, further establishing the town's early development."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1864&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1864 marks the year when the Chicago and North Western Railroad came through the village, leading to the adoption of the name 'Oregon'."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2020 CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2020 census provides demographic data for the Town of Oregon."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;2010 CENSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 2010 census provides demographic data for the Town of Oregon."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDUCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Education is mentioned as a component of the Town of Oregon, indicating its importance in the community."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OREGON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oregon is the name of the town, which was settled in 1841 and developed over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0059-1eaa521dbd55</data>
    </node>
    <edge source="&quot;RED BRICK&quot;" target="&quot;NATIONAL REGISTER OF HISTORIC PLACES&quot;">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Red Brick was added to the National Register of Historic Places by the National Register of Historic Places in 1998."</data>
      <data key="d5">"recognition, preservation"</data>
